### What issue are you seeing?

Running `/btw` fails to start a side conversation. The TUI displays:

```text
■ Failed to start side conversation: thread/fork failed during TUI bootstrap: thread/fork failed: failed to prepare paginated fork: thread-store internal error: durable rollout shrank before projection (code -32603)
```

### What steps can reproduce the bug?

1. In the existing thread `01a1205b-8ddd-7ff2-85b1-7af6709df188`, run `/btw`.
2. Observe the error above instead of a side conversation opening.

This is the observed failure sequence; a minimal standalone reproducer and regression range are not available yet.

### What is the expected behavior?

`/btw` should open a temporary side conversation from the current thread, with a separate transcript, as described in the [CLI slash command docs](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/developer-commands?surface=cli#start-a-side-chat-with-side).

### Additional information

Related reports: [#37966](https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/37966) and [#38317](https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/38317). #38317 also fails while preparing a paginated `/btw` fork, but reports an ordinal mismatch; this report has the specific `durable rollout shrank before projection` error on 0.162.0. A shared root cause has not been established.

The doctor output above is a sanitized excerpt. Installation, config loading, and state/thread-history/log database integrity checks passed; the overall report was `warning`. Local paths and unrelated checks are omitted.

